## 10 $\mathbf{X}$ -ray crystallography
Data of CR–BPY1 and CR–BPY2 were collected on a Bruker Smart APEX CCD diffractometer with graphite-monochromated Mo- $.\mathrm{K}\alpha$ $(\lambda~=~0.71073~\mathrm{~\AA~}$ using the SMART and SAINT programs.34 Their structures were determined and the heavy 15 atoms were found by direct methods using the SHELXTL-97 program package.35 Crystallographic data for them are summarized in Table 3. Except some partly occupied solvent water molecules, the other non-hydrogen atoms were refined anisotropically. Hydrogen atoms within the ligand backbones 20 were fixed geometrically at their positions and allowed to ride on the parent atoms. In both of the two structures, the ruthenium atoms were disordered in the equivalent positions of tungsten atoms. For CR–BPY2, several bond distances constraints were used to help the refinement on the BPY moiety, and thermal 25 parameters on adjacent oxygen atoms of the polyoxometalate anion were restrained to be similar.
