5 A new approach to merge Cu-catalysis/Ru-photocatalysis within one single MOF was achieved by incorporating of the photoredox catalyst $\mathrm{\Delta[SiW_{11}O_{39}R u(H_{2}O)]^{5-}}$ into the pores of $\mathrm{Cu}$ –BPY MOFs. The hybrid catalysts prompted oxidative C–C bond formation from $N.$ - phenyl-tetrahydroisoquinoline and acetophenones in high conversion and size-selectivity. The method takes advantage of visible light photoredox catalysis to generate intermediate iminium ions under mild conditions and easily combination with $\mathtt{C u}$ -catalyzed activation of nucleophiles.
